# Line endings.
#
# Text is normalised to LF in the repository; git converts it back on checkout
# where the platform wants that (core.autocrlf on Windows).
* text=auto

# Batch files are the exception in both directions. cmd.exe is handed the bytes
# that are committed, and a GitHub "Download ZIP" performs no checkout
# conversion either, so the file has to be committed the way Windows runs it.
# `-text` stores the CRLF endings verbatim instead of normalising them away,
# which keeps clones and ZIP downloads identical -- and native.
*.bat -text
